<div id="A4.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#A4.F10" title="In D.5 Image captioning (LLaVA-NeXT-7B) ‣ Appendix D Additional results ‣ Head Pursuit: Probing Attention Specialization inMultimodal Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, we report the results of our enhancing intervention on 32 color-specialized heads on Flickr30k data, while allowing the head rescaling coefficient <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> to vary between 2 and 8. The effectiveness of the intervention smoothly increases with <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, as expected. This is witnessed by the increase in the frequency of color-related words, which comes at the cost of a small decrease in the overall caption quality, measured by CIDEr (up to <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12\%</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq 5</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F10" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.21518v1/varalpha_32_propcount_bars.svg" id="A4.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/208;" width="381" height="208"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 10: </span>Effect of positive (enhancing) intervention on color-specialized heads in image captioning. Increasing the rescaling coefficient <math id="A4.F10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> leads to a stronger presence of color-related words in captions, accompanied by a gradual drop in overall caption quality as measured by CIDEr.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.T14.fig1" class="ltx_table ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:341.6pt;">
